.TH "pass\-otp" "1" "November 2026" ""
.SH NAME
pass\-otp \(em A \f[B]pass\f[R](1) extension for managing
one\-time\-password (OTP) tokens.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]pass otp\f[R] [\f[I]command\f[R]] [\f[I]options\&...\f[R]]
[\f[I]args\&...\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]pass otp\f[R] extends the \f[B]pass\f[R](1) utility with the
\f[B]otp\f[R] command for adding OTP secrets, generating OTP codes, and
displaying secret key URIs using the standard \f[I]otpauth://\f[R]
scheme.
.PP
If no \f[I]command\f[R] is specified, \f[I]command\f[R] defaults to
\f[B]code\f[R].
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]pass otp code\f[R] [ \f[CR]\-\-clip\f[R], \f[CR]\-c\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R], \f[CR]\-q\f[R] ] \f[I]pass\-name\f[R]
Generate and print an OTP code from the secret key stored in
\f[I]pass\-name\f[R] using \f[B]oathtool\f[R](1).
If \f[CR]\-\-clip\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] is specified, do not print the
code but instead copy it to the clipboard using \f[B]xclip\f[R](1) and
then restore the clipboard after 45 (or
\f[I]PASSWORD_STORE_CLIP_TIME\f[R]) seconds.
If \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R] or \f[CR]\-q\f[R] is specified, do not print the
git update message to standard out.
This command is alternatively named \f[B]show\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]pass otp insert\f[R] [ \f[CR]\-\-force\f[R], \f[CR]\-f\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-echo\f[R], \f[CR]\-e\f[R] ] [ [ \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R], \f[CR]\-s\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-issuer\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R] \f[I]issuer\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-account\f[R], \f[CR]\-a\f[R] \f[I]account\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-path\f[R], \f[CR]\-p\f[R] \f[I]path\-name\f[R] ] ] [ \f[I]pass\-name\f[R] ]
Prompt for and insert a new OTP secret into the password store at
\f[I]pass\-name\f[R].
.RS
.PP
If \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R] is specified, prompt for the \f[I]secret\f[R]
value, assuming SHA1 algorithm, 30\-second period, and 6 OTP digits.
One or both of \f[I]issuer\f[R] and \f[I]account\f[R] must also be
specified.
.PP
If \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R] is not specified, prompt for a key URI; see the
documentation at \c
.UR https://github.com/google/google-authenticator/wiki/Key-Uri-Format
.UE \c
\ for the key URI specification.
.PP
The secret is consumed from stdin; specify \f[CR]\-\-echo\f[R] or
\f[CR]\-e\f[R] to echo input when running this command interactively.
If \f[I]pass\-name\f[R] is not specified, convert the
\f[I]issuer:accountname\f[R] URI label to a path in the form of
\f[I]issuer/accountname\f[R].
Prompt before overwriting an existing secret, unless
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] or \f[CR]\-f\f[R] is specified.
This command is alternatively named \f[B]add\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]\-\-path\f[R] specifies a path prefix to the generated path from
the URI label.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]pass otp append\f[R] [ \f[CR]\-\-force\f[R], \f[CR]\-f\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-echo\f[R], \f[CR]\-e\f[R] ] [ [ \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R], \f[CR]\-s\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-issuer\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R] \f[I]issuer\f[R] ] [ \f[CR]\-\-account\f[R], \f[CR]\-a\f[R] \f[I]account\f[R] ] ] \f[I]pass\-name\f[R]
Append an OTP secret to the password stored in \f[I]pass\-name\f[R],
preserving any existing lines.
.RS
.PP
If \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R] is specified, prompt for the \f[I]secret\f[R]
value, assuming SHA1 algorithm, 30\-second period, and 6 OTP digits.
One or both of \f[I]issuer\f[R] and \f[I]account\f[R] must also be
specified.
.PP
If \f[CR]\-\-secret\f[R] is not specified, prompt for a key URI; see the
documentation at \c
.UR https://github.com/google/google-authenticator/wiki/Key-Uri-Format
.UE \c
\ for the key URI specification.
.PP
The URI is consumed from stdin; specify \f[CR]\-\-echo\f[R] or
\f[CR]\-e\f[R] to echo input when running this command interactively.
Prompt before overwriting an existing secret, unless
\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] or \f[CR]\-f\f[R] is specified.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]pass otp uri\f[R] [ \f[CR]\-\-clip\f[R], \f[CR]\-c\f[R] | \f[CR]\-\-qrcode\f[R], \f[CR]\-q\f[R] ] \f[I]pass\-name\f[R]
Print the key URI stored in \f[I]pass\-name\f[R] to stdout.
If \f[CR]\-\-clip\f[R] or \f[CR]\-c\f[R] is specified, do not print the
URI but instead copy it to the clipboard using \f[B]xclip\f[R](1) and
then restore the clipboard after 45 (or
\f[I]PASSWORD_STORE_CLIP_TIME\f[R]) seconds.
If \f[CR]\-\-qrcode\f[R] or \f[CR]\-q\f[R] is specified, do not print
the URI but instead display a QR code using \f[B]qrencode\f[R](1) either
to the terminal or graphically if supported.
.TP
\f[B]pass otp validate\f[R] \f[I]uri\f[R]
Test a URI string for validity according to the Key Uri Format.
For more information about this format, see the documentation at \c
.UR https://github.com/google/google-authenticator/wiki/Key-Uri-Format
.UE \c
\&.
